# atlas-03: a second, structurally different test of AGGR's recursive
# cue expansion (Plan 26 Phase 6) - deliberately not a copy of atlas-02,
# so a weight tuned on one case isn't mistaken for a weight that
# generalizes.
#
# The one structural difference from atlas-02: three hops, not two. The
# query's own seed entity (harbor-project) never reaches the gold entity
# (quarry-system) directly or even in one bridge - it takes two bridges
# (e1 then e2), hitting MAX_EXPANSION_ROUNDS's current cap of 3 rounds
# exactly. Everything else (fan shape, decoy count, decoy phrasing style)
# deliberately matches atlas-02, so this isolates depth as the one new
# variable.
#
# An earlier draft also widened quarry-system's fan to 3 (an extra decoy
# event mentioning it, unreachable from harbor-project) to test a worse
# fan shape at the same time. Dropped: that extra decoy shared the exact
# same spreading-activation value as the gold (same fan, same entity), so
# no weight could ever separate them - the residual gap was pure
# embedding noise on near-zero-overlap short sentences, not a graph
# signal any weight sweep can act on. Confounding two variables at once
# also would have made a failure here impossible to attribute to either
# one. Left as a separate, future dataset if fan shape needs its own test.
#
#   e1 (bridge 1) - mentions harbor-project and signal-relay. The only
#                   document reachable directly from the query's seed.
#   e2 (bridge 2) - mentions signal-relay and quarry-system. Reachable
#                   only after e1 discovers signal-relay in round 2.
#   e3 (gold)     - mentions quarry-system only, never "Harbor",
#                   "rollout", "Signal Relay", or any query word.
#                   Reachable only in round 3, seeded from quarry-system
#                   (discovered via e2 in round 2).
#   e4-e8 (decoys)- mention harbor-project only, each sharing
#                   "Harbor"/"rollout" with the question.
#
# All eight events share one timestamp - atlas-02 taught this the hard
# way: a dataset not controlled for recency confounds the very signal
# it's built to test.

